@@ -70,6 +70,24 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+It does the following:
+
+* Writes plain text, with no pretty printing of containers.
+* Does not wrap or crop output to the console width.
+* Does not apply console markup or replace emoji codes.
+* Applies highlighting by default (``highlight=True``), even if the Console disabled it. Pass ``highlight=None`` to use the Console setting, or ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off.
+* Accepts a basic ``style`` which is applied in the same way as print.
+
+Output still goes through the normal print pipeline, so render hooks, buffering, and capture work as they do for print.
+
+
